libsmb2 - SMB2/SMB3 client library
==================================

Origin:  https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2
Version: 6.2 (tag libsmb2-6.2, d67e213)
License: GNU LGPL v2.1 or later, see LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt

This is upstream's lib/ directory with its private headers next to it; the
public headers are in headers/libs/libsmb2/smb2. It is what the smbfs file
system (src/add-ons/kernel/file_systems/smbfs) talks to servers with.

Not taken over from upstream: the Kerberos wrapper (krb5-wrapper.*), which
needs a Kerberos library Haiku does not have in its build, and the ports to
other platforms. Authentication is NTLMSSP, which the library does itself.

Changes to upstream's files:
- portable-endian.h: Haiku has <endian.h>.
- libsmb2.c, smb2_open_async_with_oplock_or_lease(): files are opened
  allowing others to delete or rename them meanwhile, as POSIX has it.
- libsmb2.c, smb2_rename_async(): renaming replaces a file of the new name,
  as rename() does.

The library returns -errno and takes a negative value for a failure, so it
is built with B_USE_POSITIVE_POSIX_ERRORS. Code that uses it has to be built
with it as well, and link libposix_error_mapper.a.

config.h is written by hand in place of the one configure generates.

To update, copy lib/*.c, lib/*.h and the four private headers over these,
the public headers over those in headers/libs/libsmb2/smb2, apply the changes
listed above again, and check the list of sources in the Jamfile against
lib/CMakeLists.txt.
